    feat(aug-200): dispatch spec enrichment — board row spec_query to brief-ready CHD context
    
    Finishes the crashed 2026-11-22 AUG-200 worker residue: it left
    scripts/dispatch_spec_enrich.py and tests/test_dispatch_spec_enrich.py
    untracked in the worktree at 4 passed / 4 failed, and this commit lands both
    with the missing fix.
    
    The four failures shared one shape: on typed refusal / ambiguous paths the
    hook returned before touching --out, so the out file did not exist while the
    tests assert it exists with ZERO bytes. Fixed in
    scripts/dispatch_spec_enrich.py:
    
    - _refused (malformed spec_query, unresolvable row, unscoped/inactive spec
      task, corpus SpecError, substrate SubstrateError) now creates the --out
      file with zero bytes before returning exit 2 — never a placeholder heading,
      the refusal still surfaces on stderr and --status-json.
    - the ambiguous branch (exit 3) and the unscoped/inactive refusal branch of
      plan_section likewise leave the --out file explicitly empty.
    - module docstring's exit-code contract updated to match: the section file is
      left ZERO bytes on refusal/ambiguous (never a placeholder), the dispatch
      loop keys on the exit code and a composer that keys on the file reads an
      explicitly-empty section.
    
    Resolved behaviour: a row's detail.metadata.spec_query (project / recall /
    recall_limit / spec_task) resolves through auger.build_spec_context
    (governing blocks + closure + exclusions-with-reasons) and auger.recall
    (decision ids, store keys, scores, retrieval-tier attribution, supersession
    marks) into a brief-ready section that also embeds the row's own acceptance
    criteria; a row without spec_query is an explicit no-spec (zero bytes,
    exit 0); malformed/unresolvable queries refuse typed (exit 2); ambiguous
    spec context exits 3 with the candidate ids.
    
    Board row AUG-200 (spec-to-build loop, dispatch leg). Addresses AUG-200.
    
